sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Turing k_c at 492 nm for the 18-file Eldredgeops eye (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 88.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 runs the gamma sweep (lambda falls monotonically from 696 nm at gamma 1.2 to 341 nm at gamma 5.0, with the slot value 492 nm at gamma 2.4), the Dv/Du ratio sweep, and a simulated Du=Dv field whose standard deviation is 3.1e-5 against 0.353 for the Turing field. Otsu segmentation of the Commons eye gives foreground fraction 0.537. The KS distance between specimen and simulation radial spectra is 0.635 (reference 0). Three seeds share the nonlinear FFT bin at 574 nm (sample CV 0 on this grid). Dispersion Pearson r remains 1.0 with RMSE 3.15e-12. Image-fitness CV similarity of the 720x540 12-frame GIF against the eye photograph is 96.0. Overall 88.0/100 (faithfulness 87.6, reproducibility 88.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 6c9f67254bb352d26d4034b290d6f535a474fdb2; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/eldredgeops_rana_18file_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 6c9f67254bb352d26d4034b290d6f535a474fdb2, image/png, 430251 B, 1620×984 px, artifact_sha256 3bd1a330bd5a1ec1a555564384e620b69e8f86337fa03048551b8c0027cdb4f7 (sha256 3bd1a330bd5a1ec1a555564384e620b69e8f86337fa03048551b8c0027cdb4f7), spec_fingerprint 77967ca675ff28a543407cf6030276194492fe8aeb2e1d000397c86f88e1f90a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 77967ca675ff28a543407cf6030276194492fe8aeb2e1d000397c86f88e1f90a; artifact_sha256: 3bd1a330bd5a1ec1a555564384e620b69e8f86337fa03048551b8c0027cdb4f7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/eldredgeops_rana_18file_turing_wavelength_s0/eldredgeops_rana_18file_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=8ef91c6ae2a52449..., datasets/eldredgeops_rana_18file_turing_wavelength_s0/eldredgeops_rana_18file_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=3a83d6e639450366...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-eldredgeops-rana-18file-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 states the diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979 states the two-species reaction used here. | Eldredge 1972 documents the Middle Devonian file-count series for Phacops rana. | Clarkson, Levi-Setti and Horváth 2006 describe the schizochroal calcite eye.; reconstructed_in_script: Linear wavelength fixed at 492 nm = 4.915e-07 m for the 18-file morph at 387 Ma. | Gamma sweep showing lambda proportional to gamma^(-1/2), and an equal-diffusion field. | Otsu mask, radial-spectrum KS, and three-seed FFT wavelength on the Commons photograph. | Wavelengths per file increase by 18/17 if the arc is conserved and one file is lost by 384 Ma.; transfer_boundary: 492 nm is the assigned detail scale, not an Eldredge measurement. | The photograph is Eldredgeops rana, not a proven Cazenovian 18-file voucher.; does_not_claim: That the Schnakenberg coefficients are Devonian biochemistry. | That the eye photograph is a PDE solution or that Pearson r = 1 is a pixel fit. | That file loss retunes k_c. | A cryptographic nanopublication signature.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: No second assessor. Nanopubs are unsigned: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent and the nanopub package is not installed.",
            "remediation needed: Pearson r = 1 is the spectral mode plus RK4 on its eigenvector, not a pixel registration of the eye. The nonlinear peak sits at 574 nm.",
            "remediation needed: The Commons eye is not a stratigraphically pinned Cazenovian 18-file voucher.",
            "remediation needed: Three seeds share one radial FFT bin, so the wavelength CV on this 96^2 grid is 0." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.88"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, loop 3215)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1267-0234> .
}

